Creating a functional HTML and JavaScript application for vocabulary practice involves several components. Below is a simple implementation that includes a locally stored database using `localStorage`, editable vocabulary lists, a testing interface, a scoring system, and the option to exclude mastered vocabulary.

### HTML Structure

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Vocabulary Practice</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; }
        #vocab-list, #test-area { margin: 20px; }
        .hidden { display: none; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Vocabulary Practice</h1>

    <div id="vocab-list">
        <h2>Vocabulary List</h2>
        <textarea id="vocab-input" rows="10" cols="30" placeholder="Enter words (one per line)"></textarea><br>
        <button id="save-vocab">Save Vocabulary</button>
        <button id="load-vocab">Load Vocabulary</button>
        <button id="clear-vocab">Clear Vocabulary</button>
    </div>

    <div id="test-area" class="hidden">
        <h2>Testing Area</h2>
        <div id="question"></div>
        <input type="text" id="answer" placeholder="Your answer">
        <button id="submit-answer">Submit Answer</button>
        <div id="result"></div>
        <button id="next-question">Next Question</button>
    </div>

    <div id="score-area" class="hidden">
        <h2>Your Score: <span id="score">0</span></h2>
        <button id="restart">Restart</button>
    </div>

    <script src="app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

### JavaScript Logic (app.js)

```javascript
let vocabList = [];
let currentQuestionIndex = 0;
let score = 0;
let masteredWords = new Set();

document.getElementById('save-vocab').addEventListener('click', saveVocabulary);
document.getElementById('load-vocab').addEventListener('click', loadVocabulary);
document.getElementById('clear-vocab').addEventListener('click', clearVocabulary);
document.getElementById('submit-answer').addEventListener('click', checkAnswer);
document.getElementById('next-question').addEventListener('click', nextQuestion);
document.getElementById('restart').addEventListener('click', restartTest);

function saveVocabulary() {
    const input = document.getElementById('vocab-input').value;
    vocabList = input.split('\n').map(word => word.trim()).filter(word => word);
    localStorage.setItem('vocabList', JSON.stringify(vocabList));
    alert('Vocabulary saved!');
}

function loadVocabulary() {
    const storedVocab = localStorage.getItem('vocabList');
    if (storedVocab) {
        vocabList = JSON.parse(storedVocab);
        alert('Vocabulary loaded!');
        startTest();
    } else {
        alert('No vocabulary found!');
    }
}

function clearVocabulary() {
    localStorage.removeItem('vocabList');
    vocabList = [];
    alert('Vocabulary cleared!');
}

function startTest() {
    document.getElementById('vocab-list').classList.add('hidden');
    document.getElementById('test-area').classList.remove('hidden');
    document.getElementById('score-area').classList.add('hidden');
    currentQuestionIndex = 0;
    score = 0;
    nextQuestion();
}

function nextQuestion() {
    if (currentQuestionIndex < vocabList.length) {
        const word = vocabList[currentQuestionIndex];
        document.getElementById('question').innerText = `What is the meaning of: ${word}?`;
        document.getElementById('answer').value = '';
        document.getElementById('result').innerText = '';
    } else {
        endTest();
    }
}

function checkAnswer() {
    const answer = document.getElementById('answer').value.trim();
    // Here you can implement a more complex answer checking logic
    if (answer.toLowerCase() === 'correct answer') { // Replace with actual answer checking
        score++;
        masteredWords.add(vocabList[currentQuestionIndex]);
        document.getElementById('result').innerText = 'Correct!';
    } else {
        document.getElementById('result').innerText = 'Incorrect!';
    }
    currentQuestionIndex++;
    nextQuestion();
}

function endTest() {
    document.getElementById('test-area').classList.add('hidden');
    document.getElementById('score-area').classList.remove('hidden');
    document.getElementById('score').innerText = score;
}

function restartTest() {
    masteredWords.clear();
    startTest();
}
```

### Explanation

1. **HTML Structure**: The HTML contains sections for vocabulary input, testing, and score display. It uses buttons to trigger actions and a textarea for input.

2. **JavaScript Logic**:
   - **Vocabulary Management**: Users can save, load, and clear vocabulary lists using `localStorage`.
   - **Testing Interface**: The application presents a word and checks the user's answer. The correct answer checking logic can be customized.
   - **Scoring System**: The score is tracked and displayed at the end of the test.
   - **Mastered Vocabulary**: The application allows users to exclude mastered vocabulary by keeping track of correct answers.

### Usage
1. Enter vocabulary words in the textarea (one per line) and click "Save Vocabulary".
2. Click "Load Vocabulary" to start the testing interface.
3. Answer the questions and check your score at the end.

This is a basic implementation. You can enhance it by adding features like:
- A more sophisticated answer checking mechanism.
- A way to define correct answers for each vocabulary word.
- A user interface for managing mastered vocabulary.
- Styling improvements for better user experience.

